"w": "A snapshot is a point-in-time backup of one EBS volume , stored by AWS (in S3, behind the scenes). Snapshots are incremental : after the first, only changed blocks are saved. Restore a snapshot as a new volume in any AZ , or copy it to another Region for disaster recovery. Archive tier cuts storage cost up to 75%; the Recycle Bin catches accidental deletes. Walkthrough: one snapshot, five uses Incremental snapshot lab Which snapshot feature?"
