"d": "Angular 22: CareDesk's PatientList hands a patient down to PatientCard with input(), the card reports back with output(), and a nurse's note syncs both ways with model(). Plus why mutating an object inside a signal does nothing.",
"w": "Data goes down through inputs: the card declares patient = input.required<Patient>() , the list binds [patient]=\"patient()\" . Events go up through outputs: the card calls reviewed.emit(…) , the list listens with (reviewed)=\"onReviewed($event)\" . Two-way binding is both at once: note = model('') in the card, [(note)]=\"note\" in the list. Inputs are read-only signals : read them with patient() , derive with computed , react with effect . A change means a new object . Changing a property of the same"
